tests:
  unit:
    count: 46
    detail: "ui/src/setup.test.ts +9 — the sixteen short forms asserted LITERALLY against design run #9's table, not merely for existence: one case per verdict for the value and its remedy, one asserting every short is <=40 chars (StatusLine's anatomy cap, the reason the field exists), one proving the two error verdicts do NOT interpolate into the short form (a 500-character error still yields 'install failed' / 'couldn't set the proxy' — the unbounded case the [UI_DEFER] marker named), one proving `message` is unchanged so the field is an addition rather than a replacement, and a count assertion that the table is 16 so a new verdict cannot be added without landing here. ui/src/components/StatusLine.test.tsx 17 -> 23 — the extend's own contract: the message carries the verdict tone for ok and warn while muted stays ink-mute (three cases), it renders `short` and NOT the full sentence, and it refuses to render `remedy` (the split is the point — a verdict and an instruction are two elements). The eleven pre-existing tests were updated, not deleted: their literals gained `short` and their assertions moved to the fragment. ui/src/components/Checkbox.test.tsx NEW, 5 — reports the boolean not the event, holds no value of its own, the label is inside the hit target (clicking the words toggles it), disabled reports nothing, and no indeterminate state exists. ui/src/components/CopyText.test.tsx 7 -> 9 — the error state this WU added: a refused write says 'copy failed' and clears on the same ~2s timer as the confirm. ui/src/Onboarding.test.tsx 19 -> 24, REWRITTEN to the new surface with every old assertion's intent preserved; the rewrite is evidence in itself, since the deleted 'Next moves the active step forward' maps to a design line that deleted the control. New coverage the old file could not have: no Back/Next pair exists, one body is open at a time, a failed action force-opens the manual Disclosure via defaultOpen (DEC-21 — the native element owns its state), a long verdict keeps the fragment on the line while its remedy renders in a separate Notice, and the clipboard both confirms and reports failure where the old calls were unguarded."
  integration:
    count: 28
    detail: "ui/src/ProxyCloseDialog.test.tsx NEW — the file did not exist; the app's only modal, and the only screen that can strand a machine with no internet, had no test at all. Its bounded contract, the part no unit test reaches because it is about mode branching and focus ownership: all three modes' action sets (ours/foreign actionable, remote info-only); that 'keep' is gone as a second name for quitting, asserted both as a missing control and as absent copy; the remedy's failure relabelling the SAME slot to 'try again' rather than stranding a retry button, with quit still one click away (the never-trap invariant, relocated from closeConfirm where it used to be satisfied by quitting onto a dead proxy); try again re-running the remedy; the opt-out reaching onAcknowledge with its value, and never being offered where something local can be fixed; the exit being the same bare quit in every mode; and the modal shell — Esc, backdrop and dismiss each cancelling in each of the three modes (9 cases), focus entering the panel on open, focus RETURNING to the invoker on unmount, and Tab trapped inside. ui/src/closeConfirm.test.tsx 12 -> 10 — the two dialog tests moved to the new file where they belong; the hook's own tests were updated to the three-mode model, and one existing test was deliberately inverted (see waived/notes)."
  e2e:
    count: 3
    detail: "ui/e2e/specs/onboarding.spec.ts +2, and one renamed. The spec was NOT rewritten wholesale: its selectors survived the rebuild because the step containers kept their data-testid, so the spine is untouched (fresh launch -> onboarding -> a real decrypted HTTPS flow through the real proxy -> the list revealed -> filter narrows -> live append). The two additions prove what the redesign IS, against the real Tauri window: every step carries a verdict (all three status elements exist) and NO prev/next pair exists — the navigation the design deliberately removed is as much the contract as the verdicts it kept; and a step opens from its own header with exactly one body open. Hermetic: ephemeral ports, the harness's own local origin, no public network."
